  <justification>
    <existing>src/solutions/EventDetailSidePane/src/components/MemoSection.tsx — same sprk_memo CRUD but embedded in EventDetailSidePane layout, single-memo model.</existing>
    <extension>MemoSection isn't shaped as a reusable code-page (no list, no `+`, no dropdown, no popover, embedded not launched). Extracting CRUD to a hook is a clean improvement.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Notepad would either fork MemoSection (anti-pattern) OR not ship. §11 catches forking.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Design API (REVISED per task 001): interface UseSprkMemoRepository { memos: Memo[]; loading; error; unsupported: boolean; currentMemo: Memo | null; setCurrentMemo(id); createMemo(): Promise&lt;Memo | null&gt;; updateBody(body: string, options?: { immediate?: boolean }): void; updateName(name: string): void; }</step>
    <step order="2">Look up entity-specific lookup field name from SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS (from toolbarLaunchDefaults). If regardingEntity not in map, set unsupported=true and skip queries.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement list: Xrm.WebApi.retrieveMultipleRecords("sprk_memo", `?$filter=_${lookupField}_value eq ${regardingId}&amp;$select=sprk_memoid,sprk_name,sprk_memobody,sprk_regardingrecordid,createdby,createdon,modifiedon&amp;$orderby=createdon desc`).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement create: import { applyResolverFields } from "@spaarke/ui-components"; discover nav-props for sprk_memo (via ManyToOneRelationships metadata query — cache); resolve parent record name via Xrm.WebApi.retrieveRecord($select=primary-name-field for the parent entity); call applyResolverFields(webApi, entity, navProps, regardingEntity, entitySetName(regardingEntity), regardingId, parentName); add sprk_name = "Untitled"; add sprk_memobody = ""; call Xrm.WebApi.createRecord("sprk_memo", entity); refetch list; setCurrentMemo(new id).</step>
    <step order="5">Implement updateBody with debounce (1000ms) via a ref-held timer; options.immediate cancels timer + writes now via Xrm.WebApi.updateRecord("sprk_memo", currentMemo.sprk_memoid, { sprk_memobody: body }).</step>
    <step order="6">Implement updateName: immediate write of sprk_name via Xrm.WebApi.updateRecord.</step>
    <step order="5">Handle Xrm undefined (test env) gracefully.</step>
    <step order="6">Write tests: list order; create returns new id; debounced update coalesces rapid keystrokes; immediate=true triggers immediate write.</step>
    <step order="7">Run tests.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 033 ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/Notepad/src/hooks/useSprkMemoRepository.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/Notepad/src/hooks/__tests__/useSprkMemoRepository.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">list retrieveMultipleRecords URL contains sprk_regardingrecordid eq 'guid' filter and $orderby=createdon desc.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">create issues a single createRecord call with sprk_regardingrecordid set and empty sprk_body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given rapid keystrokes, updateBody debounces to a single write after 1s idle.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given options={immediate:true}, updateBody writes immediately regardless of debounce timer.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Debounce ref MUST be cleared on unmount to avoid stale writes. Field name sprk_body assumed per spec Assumptions; if 001 reveals a different name, update accordingly.</notes>

